945:(Grab her hand!)
946:The moment my hand closes around hers, time seems to slow to a crawl.
947:The starling takes wing, the chipmunk clings to the fox's ears, and the fox grips Yuzu's magical vine – yet its bushy tail brushes the mirrorlike surface of the lake.
948:Ripples spread across the lake. Our frantic reflections melt away, replaced by scenes both intimate and unfamiliar –
949:A younger Yuzu stands at the edge of the forest, a small bindle slung over her shoulder.//nThe animals gather around her in tearful farewell as she waves goodbye and turns to leave.
