951:Wait... what's this?
952:After her departure, the vision shifts to an aging fox.
953:Though frail, it moves with quiet grace, climbing to the ridge at the forest's edge every day to gaze into the distance.
954:Until one day, it can no longer make the climb.//nWith great care, it passes the enchanted leaf worn on its chest to a young cub.
955:An elderly starling, wings too weary for flight, teaches a hatchling where the sweetest berries grow;//nan aged chipmunk shows a tiny kit the secret burrows where winter nuts are stashed...
957:This is...
